<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mala Khortytsia</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Baida Island</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mala Khortytsia is a small island in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dnieper">Dnieper</a> river at Zaporizhzhia, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>, west of the larger island of Khortytsia. Around 1552 Prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dmytro-vyshnevetsky">Dmytro Vyshnevetsky</a> built a wooden fortress there, whose remains have been excavated, and it is often seen as the site of the first Zaporozhian Sich. It is also called Baida Island after him.</p></div>
